-`ctx.function_call.call_id` inside a conversation tool and on `ctx.task_id`
-inside a task, so a repeated call is a no-op on the other side.
+A tool may run again after a retry, and in text a run may be lost after its
+tools ran: its worker died (`worker-lost`) or its save failed
+(`storage-unavailable`), and the client resends the message under a new
+`messageId`. A step's calls are in the thread before their tools run
+([storage.md](storage.md)), so the next run's model reads each call of the
+lost run that has no result as not finished, its outcome unknown.
+
+Key every outside call on `ctx.idempotency_key(ref)`, where `ref` names the
+effect, such as an order number or a room and its dates. The key is the same
+for the same thread, tool and `ref` on every run, so a call that a lost run
+made and the next run makes again is a no-op on the other side; two effects
+need two refs. `ctx.function_call.call_id` and `ctx.task_id` are new on every
+run.
 
